    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d633-a10">

                <pb facs="0756" n="670" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg670"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 7.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Algara to Mr. Clayton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-10-08"><hi rendition="#italic">October 8,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Ambassador</hi>: Referring to the note of the 3d
                    instant, in which, by instruction of your Government, your excellency is pleased
                    to urge the prosecution of the persons <pb facs="0757" n="671" xml:id="pg671"/>
                    supposed to be guilty of the murder of certain American citizens in the
                    Republic, I have the honor to say, in regard to the case of Philip Nesdel, that
                    this department has received no later information than that which was
                    communicated to your excellency on December 22 of last year; but I have asked
                    the governor of the State of Jalisco for a further report, and I have requested
                    him to direct that more active efforts be made to effect the arrest of one of
                    the murderers of Nesdel who has not yet been captured.</p>
                <p>I beg to renew, etc.,</p>
                <p>In the absence of the secretary, the subsecretary,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">José Algara.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
